{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.JetHorizon","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.JetHorizon","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic"],"declarations":56,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qou_is_ccc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qou_is_ccc","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L285-L312","doc":"**QOU is CCC — horizon-local form.**\n\nAt any jet horizon, the three horizon-local CCC properties\nhold: degree-0 sections vanish, and non-trivial degree-1\nand degree-2 sections persist.  This is the\n`prop:qou-is-ccc` content that follows from the\n`JetHorizon` structure axioms alone (CCC-1 and CCC-3 of\nthe .md narrative).\n\nNote (PR #776): the *full* `prop:qou-is-ccc` claim in the\nnarrative also asserts **CCC-2 — boundary-data\ninheritance** (the CMB of an aeon equals the terminal\nboundary datum of its adjacent predecessor; see\n`def:cmb-boundary-datum` and `def:aeon` adjacency).  That\npiece requires a CMB-of-aeon construction beyond\n`JetHorizon`'s field structure and is not yet formalised\nhere — the `(chain, h_adj, hH)` hypotheses of the previous\nformulation were unused (Copilot, PR #776).  Tracking the\nCCC-2 piece as conditional-class follow-up work. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:qou-is-ccc","label":"prop:qou-is-ccc","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/qou-is-ccc.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ccc_boundary_data_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ccc_boundary_data_exists","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L280-L283","doc":"**CCC property 2**: at each horizon, degree ≥ 1 data persists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ccc_conformal_invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ccc_conformal_invariance","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L275-L278","doc":"**CCC property 1**: at each horizon, all degree-0 sections vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.horizon_conformal_invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.horizon_conformal_invariance","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L247-L271","doc":"**Degree-0 vanishing at the jet horizon** — the algebraic\nprecondition underlying `prop:horizon-conformal-invariance`.\n\nEvery degree-0 section vanishes at a jet horizon, by the\n`JetHorizon.degree_zero_vanishes` field.  This is the direct\nstatement provable from the abstract `JetHorizon` interface.\n\nThe full conformal-invariance consequence stated in the .md\nnarrative — that the boundary datum\n`(A_1 / A_0, A_2 / A_0)|_{H}` is invariant under rescaling\n`A_0 ↦ λ A_0` for any unit `λ` on the horizon — follows\nbecause the quotient `A_k / λ A_0` depends only on the\nideal generated by vanishing degree-0 sections (i.e. on\nthe *vanishing locus*, not on the specific generator).\nStating that consequence formally requires a `Module` /\nquotient structure on each `A_k` that the abstract\n`JetHorizon` interface does not (yet) carry; see the .md\nnarrative for the categorical proof sketch. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:horizon-conformal-invariance","label":"prop:horizon-conformal-invariance","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/horizon-conformal-invariance.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.planckStepResult_cmb_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.planckStepResult_cmb_independent","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L231-L243","doc":"**The removed axiom's statement, discharged — and shown to ignore its\nown argument.**  `fun _ => toyResult` has exactly the type the axiom had,\nand it returns the same result for any two CMB inputs.  Any future\nstatement of aeon recycling must constrain a Planck-step map; a bare\n`CMBFunctorValue → PlanckStepResult` carries no content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.planckStepResult_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.planckStepResult_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L224-L229","doc":"`PlanckStepResult` is inhabited, with no appeal to the recycling\nconjecture.  Refutes the removed axiom's stated justification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.toyGradedJetAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.toyGradedJetAlgebra","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L217-L222","doc":"A toy graded jet algebra — `ULift Bool` at every degree, zero is `false`.\nExists only as the witness for the two vacuity theorems below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PlanckStepResult.degree_one_inherited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PlanckStepResult.degree_one_inherited","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L171-L171","doc":"The degree-1 data is inherited from the CMB. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PlanckStepResult.degree_zero_regenerated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PlanckStepResult.degree_zero_regenerated","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L169-L169","doc":"The new algebra has non-trivial degree-0 sections. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PlanckStepResult.next_algebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PlanckStepResult.next_algebra","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L167-L167","doc":"The new graded jet algebra after the Planck step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PlanckStepResult.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PlanckStepResult.mk","kind":"ctor","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L165-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PlanckStepResult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PlanckStepResult","kind":"structure","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L162-L171","doc":"The result of applying one Planck step to CMB data:\na new graded jet algebra (the next aeon's algebra) that has\nnon-trivial degree-0 sections regenerated from the degree-1 CMB data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBFunctorValue.algebra_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBFunctorValue.algebra_match","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L158-L158","doc":"The CMB's algebra matches the horizon's algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBFunctorValue.cmb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBFunctorValue.cmb","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L156-L156","doc":"The CMB data at this horizon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBFunctorValue.in_boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBFunctorValue.in_boundary","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L154-L154","doc":"The horizon is in the aeon's boundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBFunctorValue.horizon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBFunctorValue.horizon","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L152-L152","doc":"The boundary horizon from which CMB data is extracted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBFunctorValue.source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBFunctorValue.source","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L150-L150","doc":"The source aeon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBFunctorValue.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBFunctorValue.mk","kind":"ctor","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L148-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBFunctorValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBFunctorValue","kind":"structure","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L144-L158","doc":"The CMB functor value: the degree ≥ 1 data surviving a\nboundary horizon. Composition of ∂ with the colimit of\n(A_1/A_0 ⊕ A_2/A_0) over the boundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.horizonFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.horizonFunctor","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L140-L142","doc":"The horizon functor: sends an aeon to its boundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.adjacent","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L133-L136","doc":"Two aeons are adjacent if their boundaries share a common\njet horizon: ∂𝒜₁ ∩ ∂𝒜₂ ≠ ∅. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Aeon.boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Aeon.boundary","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L131-L131","doc":"Boundary: jet horizons reachable as limits of directed\ndiagrams in the aeon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Aeon.connected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Aeon.connected","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L124-L124","doc":"Connectedness: any two configs are related by a chain of\nflow steps.  This is the transitive closure of flow_step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Aeon.flow_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Aeon.flow_symm","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L121-L121","doc":"The flow relation is symmetric (reversible computation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Aeon.flow_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Aeon.flow_step","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L119-L119","doc":"A relation witnessing that two configs are connected by a\nflow map (one Planck step) within Bun°. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Aeon.observable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Aeon.observable","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L116-L116","doc":"Each configuration is observable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Aeon.configs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Aeon.configs","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L114-L114","doc":"The observable configurations in this aeon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Aeon.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Aeon.mk","kind":"ctor","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Aeon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Aeon","kind":"structure","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L107-L131","doc":"An aeon: a connected component of the observable subcategory\nBun°(P(V)).  Maximal collection of observable configurations\nconnected by flow maps without crossing a jet horizon. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:aeon","label":"def:aeon","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/aeon.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ObservableConfig.degree_zero_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ObservableConfig.degree_zero_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L105-L105","doc":"There exists a non-trivial degree-0 section. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ObservableConfig.algebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ObservableConfig.algebra","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L103-L103","doc":"The graded jet algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ObservableConfig.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ObservableConfig.mk","kind":"ctor","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ObservableConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ObservableConfig","kind":"structure","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L97-L105","doc":"The observable subcategory Bun°(P(V)): configurations where\nthe degree-0 algebra is non-trivial (Frobenius pairing\nnon-degenerate on A_0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.degree_two_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.degree_two_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The degree-2 section is non-trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.degree_two_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.degree_two_witness","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L91-L91","doc":"A non-trivial degree-2 section (curvature mode). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.degree_one_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.degree_one_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The degree-1 section is non-trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.degree_one_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.degree_one_witness","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L87-L87","doc":"A non-trivial degree-1 section (winding mode). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.source","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The big bang state whose CMB this is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CMBBoundaryDatum","kind":"structure","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L80-L93","doc":"The CMB (cosmic microwave background) of a big bang state:\nthe degree ≥ 1 jet data that survives the degree-0 vanishing. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:cmb-boundary-datum","label":"def:cmb-boundary-datum","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/cmb-boundary-datum.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BigBangState.nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BigBangState.nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L78-L78","doc":"At least one base point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BigBangState.numBasePoints","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BigBangState.numBasePoints","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Number of base points in the initial configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BigBangState.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BigBangState.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BigBangState.toJetHorizon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BigBangState.toJetHorizon","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L74-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BigBangState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BigBangState","kind":"structure","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L67-L78","doc":"A big bang state: a bundle initial condition where A_0 = 0.\nAlgebraically identical to a jet horizon but used as a\nreference configuration rather than a boundary.\n\nExistence is not assumed: whether any affine chart admits\na big bang state is a dynamical question. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:big-bang-state","label":"def:big-bang-state","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/big-bang-state.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetHorizon.degree_two_leaks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetHorizon.degree_two_leaks","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L65-L65","doc":"There exists a non-trivial degree-2 section at the horizon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetHorizon.degree_one_leaks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetHorizon.degree_one_leaks","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L63-L63","doc":"There exists a non-trivial degree-1 section at the horizon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetHorizon.degree_zero_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetHorizon.degree_zero_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L61-L61","doc":"At the horizon, every degree-0 section equals zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetHorizon.algebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetHorizon.algebra","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The graded jet algebra over the chart. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetHorizon.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetHorizon.mk","kind":"ctor","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetHorizon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetHorizon","kind":"structure","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L51-L65","doc":"A jet horizon in an affine chart: a locus where the degree-0\nalgebra A_0 vanishes.  The horizon ideal h ⊂ Γ(U, A_0) blocks\nall zeroth-order sections; higher-degree jet data (A_k/A_0 for\nk ≥ 1) can carry non-trivial sections across the horizon. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:jet-horizon","label":"def:jet-horizon","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/jet-horizon.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedJetAlgebra.inclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedJetAlgebra.inclusion","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Inclusion A_k ↪ A_{k+1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedJetAlgebra.zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedJetAlgebra.zero","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The zero section at each degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedJetAlgebra.sections","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedJetAlgebra.sections","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The type of sections at degree k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedJetAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedJetAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedJetAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedJetAlgebra","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/JetHorizon.lean#L39-L47","doc":"A graded jet algebra: type family indexed by degree k ∈ ℕ,\nwith sections at each degree. ","signatureChunk":0}]}